  "lineage": "Gamelan tradition of the Cirebon courts (Kasepuhan and Kanoman) on the north coast of West Java, played on paired sets in prawa, a five-tone tuning, and pelog. It serves court ceremonies, topeng Cirebon masked dance and wayang, and the region also keeps antique ensembles such as gamelan sekaten (gong sekati), gong renteng and denggung.",
